{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>And we struck every city of men, and the women and the little ones</b> — for they were of the Amorites, and they were commanded in this, as it is stated (Deuteronomy 20:16): \"Only of the cities of these peoples that HaShem your Elohim gives you for an inheritance, you shall not let any soul live.\" Yet even so, He opened to them with peace, for such is the commandment, as I shall explain with the help of Heaven (Ramban on Deuteronomy 20:10). But to Og king of Bashan he did not call for peace, because he came out to meet them in battle before they reached his city at all. I have already explained the matter in the portion of Zot Chukkat (Numbers 21:21)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The lemma words מתם appear to combine מת (men) with the suffix ם, possibly a manuscript abbreviation or contraction; rendered hyper-literally as 'of men.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:44:36.350737279Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}